    <h2 id="how-it-flows">How it flows</h2>
    <ol class="flow">
      <li><code>POST /notes</code> creates a note in <strong>notes-api</strong>. The endpoint enqueues a FastAPI <code>BackgroundTask</code> to classify and tag it. The <code>201</code> returns immediately. The task runs after notes-api sends the response.</li>
      <li>The <strong>background task</strong> POSTs the note text to the classifier's <code>/classify</code> endpoint.</li>
      <li>The <strong>classifier</strong> classifies the text into a category, an operational domain, and a region. It returns them. One Sonnet call does the work, and tool-use forces the structured output.</li>
      <li>The task writes the labels back as namespaced tags (<code>PUT /notes/&#123;id&#125;/tags</code>, replace semantics). It preserves the user's own tags. It maps all three fields. It mapped only the first two until 2026-07-18, because the region field was newer than this consumer. An unset <code>CLASSIFIER_URL</code> makes the whole step a no-op.</li>
      <li>The <strong>kb-agent</strong> reads notes (<code>GET /notes</code>) to ground its RAG answers, and can also call the classifier synchronously.</li>
    </ol>


